---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Banyan from '../components/art/Banyan.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { parts, figuresInPart, lifespan, figureHref, href, nodes } from '../lib/graph.js';

const written = new Set((await getCollection('figures')).map((e) => e.id));
const people = nodes.filter((n) => n.tier === 'chapter' || n.tier === 'profile');
const nChapters = nodes.filter((n) => n.tier === 'chapter').length;
const nProfiles = nodes.filter((n) => n.tier === 'profile').length;
---
<Base current="contents">
<main class="wrap">
  <header class="hero">
    <div>
      <span class="label">A web book</span>
      <h1>{site.title}</h1>
      <p class="sub">{site.subtitle}. Thirteen questions, {nChapters} chapters, {nProfiles} profiles, and one tree that connects them.</p>
    </div>
    <Banyan label="Illustration: a banyan tree, whose aerial roots become new trunks" />
  </header>

  <div class="col">
    <p>A banyan sends roots down from its branches, and over the years those roots thicken into trunks of their own. Modern Indian spirituality grew in much the same way. This book follows it from the 1830s to the present, one person at a time: their life, what they taught, what they added to the traditions they inherited, and where they sit on the lineage tree.</p>
    <p>Each of the thirteen parts asks one question. You can read the book straight through, or start from the <a href={href('/tree/')}>tree</a> and follow a branch that interests you.</p>

    <h2>Contents</h2>
    <ul class="toc">
      <li class="chapter-entry"><span><a href={href('/prologue/')}>Prologue: The Roots</a><span class="tier-tag written">Draft ready</span></span><span class="yrs">800 BCE–1830</span></li>
    </ul>

    {parts.map((p) => {
      const figs = figuresInPart(p.n).filter((f) => f.tier === 'chapter' || f.tier === 'profile');
      return (
        <section style="margin-top:2.2rem">
          <a href={href(`/parts/${p.slug}/`)} style="text-decoration:none;color:inherit">
            <span class="label">Part {p.n} · {p.title}</span>
            <h3 style="margin:.2rem 0 .6rem;font-size:1.35rem">{p.question}</h3>
          </a>
          <ul class="toc">
            {figs.map((f) => (
              <li class={f.tier === 'chapter' ? 'chapter-entry' : ''}>
                <span><a href={figureHref(f.id)}>{f.name}</a>{written.has(f.id) && <span class="tier-tag written">Draft ready</span>}</span>
                <span class="yrs">{lifespan(f)}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </section>
      );
    })}

    <ul class="toc" style="margin-top:2.2rem">
      <li class="chapter-entry"><span><a href={href('/epilogue/')}>Epilogue: Reading the Tree</a><span class="tier-tag">Outline</span></span><span class="yrs"></span></li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin-top:2rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem">Bold entries are full chapters; the rest are shorter profiles. {people.length} figures in all, plus many more on the tree.</p>
  </div>
</main>
</Base>
